<title>UK: UK clears Carlton acquisition of Westcountry.</title>
<headline>UK clears Carlton acquisition of Westcountry.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Department of Trade and Industry said on Monday it had decided not to refer Carlton Communications Plc's acquisition of Westcountry Television Ltd to the Monopolies and Merger Commission.  </p>
<p>Carlton said last November it had beaten off rival United News &amp; Media Plc to take control of privately-owned Westcountry.</p>
<p>Carlton made an agreed 85 million stg bid for Westcountry. The deal makes Carlton Britain's biggest independent television company.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
